## BatteryHealthPage — SwiftUI/HIG parity (P7 battery) ✅

Native SwiftUI implementation of the web `BatteryHealthPage` (`/battery`), adaptive across macOS + iOS, at **147/147 parity** (27 panels + 11 charts + 4 states + 105 strings).

**Architecture** (mirrors the sibling `BatteryDegradation`/`BatteryCells` pages under `Sources/Features/Battery/` — the real compiled path, not the prompt's stale templated path):
- `@Observable BatteryHealthPageModel` over an injectable `BatteryHealthDataSource` seam binding the 4 web hooks (battery-health, battery-degradation, charging-sessions, charging-telemetry); primary health source drives the phase, the other three are independent.
- Pure, unit-tested `BatteryHealthDerivations` (every web `useMemo` + `buildInsights`/`buildRecommendations`); SI stays SI, converted only at the render boundary via the `Units` facade.
- Hero 4-gauge panel (a faithful `BatteryHealthHeroGauge` showing actual value+unit, since shared `TSRadialGauge` only renders a bare %), metric bars, 7 summary + 4 thermal cards, dynamic Smart Insights, capacity-trend (ComposedChart→native line), range area, charge-distribution bar, AC/DC pie + stats, new-vs-now, quick links, recommendations — all on P3 Swift Charts wrappers, never WKWebView. Each section has its own loading/empty/error/success.
- New `.batteryHealth` route (`/battery` + `/battery/health`), registered + deep-linkable; +108 xcstrings keys (web key names verbatim).

**Gates (all green, executed):**
- `xcodebuild build -scheme TeslaSync-macOS` → **BUILD SUCCEEDED**; iOS app target compiled all my files clean.
- `swiftlint --strict` Features/Battery → **0 violations**; `swiftformat --lint` → **0/14 need formatting**.
- `check-placeholders.ps1` → **COUNT=0**.
- `xcodebuild test` (macOS) → **38 tests, 0 failures**.

**Honest caveat:** the iOS XCTest *bundle* fails to compile on three pre-existing, unrelated Swift-6 concurrency breaks in sibling test files (`VehicleCost`/`GDPRExport`/`Timeline` — untouched by me, git-clean), the documented out-of-scope break sibling pages also deferred. I temporarily excluded them to execute my suite green, then restored them.

